phase P2
title Test system
description
    **Class:** not readily verifiable.

    **Kind:** verification-suite.

    **Goal:** Flow's own tests run on Flow's own test tooling (Story, Fake, the runtime cut, the trace, the CLI); the
    hand cases are ported onto it and the bridge is deleted. Decided by the user on 2026-11-15. The tools' API is
    @plan.Testing as set out in code:wiki/plans/flow/references/proposals/test-tooling-reuse-2026-11-15.md; the strategy
    and evidence are in code:wiki/plans/flow/references/proposals/test-system-2026-11-15.md, except the parts the reuse
    proposal supersedes.

    **Guides:** the reference apps' stories, tests and fakes show the intended shape; the Plan wins where they differ.
    New fixtures come from code:wiki/plans/flow/references/proposals/fixture-catalogue-2026-11-11.md (shapes S01 to S29,
    usual and stress) and the ui-sdk waves (@task.V3.T71, @task.V3.T72, @task.V3.T73); each feature Task builds the
    shapes its feature unlocks (the user, 2026-11-16). Known stale there: `ensure` or `useActorByRef` with input,
    `signal` in contexts, no `services:`, persistence `version`, CLI strings, `Fake.fetch` (now `Fake.http`), `drop({
    times })` (later, @task.V3.T29), `Fake.storage.write.hold({ match })` (now `Fake.storage` with `hold`), and any line
    saying fixtures shadow setup services (they replace them). Link:
    code:wiki/plans/flow/references/checkout/features/Pay/pay.story.ts,
    code:wiki/plans/flow/references/checkout/features/Pay/pay.test.ts,
    code:wiki/plans/flow/references/checkout/features/Cart/cart.story.ts,
    code:wiki/plans/flow/references/checkout/features/Refunds/refunds.story.ts,
    code:wiki/plans/flow/references/checkout/testing/stripe.fake.ts,
    code:wiki/plans/flow/references/checkout/testing/checkout.property.test.ts,
    code:wiki/plans/flow/references/checkout/adapters/server.ts,
    code:wiki/plans/flow/references/checkout/flow.config.ts,
    code:wiki/plans/flow/references/dispatch-desk/testing/desk.fake.ts,
    code:wiki/plans/flow/references/dispatch-desk/testing/desk.property.test.ts,
    code:wiki/plans/flow/references/dispatch-desk/tools/inspection.ts,
    code:wiki/plans/flow/references/dispatch-desk/flow.config.ts, and each app's `features/*/*.story.ts` and
    `*.test.ts`. Not guides: `*.contracts.ts`, setup and persistence files, `tools/cli.ts`, `tools/diagnostics.ts`, the
    READMEs, `REVIEW.md`, `REWRITE-PLAN.md` and `typecheck/standin/`.

    **Folder structure** (`packages/flow-state-v3/`; the Task that builds each part in brackets):

    ```text
    src/core/                  pure core, unchanged
    src/host/runtime.ts        runtimeSetup keeps its config under an internal key so a Story boots it [T63]
    src/host/inspect.ts        inspect(runtime), the runtime cut [T63]; inspect(app) [T49]
    src/host/trace.ts          run.trace, render(trace, "text") [T65]
    src/host/cli/main.ts       main(argv), called by the flow bin [T69]
    src/host/store.ts          Store as a port [T58]
    src/host/testing/          flow-state/testing, exported by T29; Flow's tests use it by path until then
      story.ts                 Story.app chained, Story.Step [T63]
      run.ts                   the one runner: TestClock, Effect's scheduler, a page per reload [T63]
      fake.ts                  Fake.server, Fake.call, Fake.control, Fake.world, Fake.Lost, Fake.storage [T63]
      config.ts                defineConfig, first slice [T69]
      index.ts
      page.ts                  deleted [T67]; the src/host/testing.ts seam moves in here, unexported [T67]
    fixtures/<name>/           contracts.ts (port, operations), machine.ts (machine, app, setup, refs),
                               server.ts (Fake.server, port fake Layer), stories.ts;
                               optional <port>-http.ts (production adapter) and <port>.contract.ts
    tests/<spec area>/         Story tests by Spec area; tests/stories (the tooling's own) [T63]
    tests/rules/               run rules and the reload sweep [T64]
    tests/types/               compile-time tests [T68]
    tests/cli/                 CLI tests over flow.config.ts [T69]
    tests/generated/           propertyTest runs [T70]
    tests/faults.ts            planted faults
    bench/run.ts               times run() over the long Stories [T66]
    flow.config.ts             lists Flow's own fixtures, the same file an app keeps [T69]
    ```

    **Starts when:** now, ahead of every remaining core slice. P3 starts only after this phase's completion audit.

    **Order:** @task.V3.T62, @task.V3.T63, @task.V3.T64, @task.V3.T65, @task.V3.T66, @task.V3.T67, @task.V3.T68,
    @task.V3.T69, @task.V3.T71, @task.V3.T70, @task.V3.T75. Where several are ready, take the earliest in this order.

    **Verified by:**

    - the suite: the Story tests under `packages/flow-state-v3/tests/`, with the run rules and the reload sweep, run by
      `vp test`; the builder runs it, and a lead that did not build it audits it (skill:policy-testing#audit-a-suite);
    - its mutants: `nub run faults` plants a dead core and each named fault of
      code:packages/flow-state-v3/tests/faults.ts in a scratch copy, one at a time;
    - its coverage record: written by @task.V3.T67 and proposed as a verification entry of @plan.Runtime, which is a
      Plan edit and so the user's yes; until then it is a comment on this phase;
    - skill:check-task per Task; `nub run check` and `nub run lint:rules` at zero.

    **One iteration:** the next ready Task: write its checks and see them fail, build, run the suite and `nub run
    faults`, then an independent skill:check-task. Findings are gathered by root cause before the next Task.

    **Exit criteria:**

    - every Task is done, and `tests/bridge/` is deleted, so one test style is left;
    - everything under "Prove" in skill:policy-verification holds at the final revision: the suite runs end to end, the
      dead core and every named fault are caught, and the audit has passed;
    - the coverage record exists.

    **False pass:** a harness made of the product hiding the product's bugs; a ported test that asserts less than the
    case it replaces.

    **Caught by:** the fault run and the dead core; the pure core tests beside the core
    (code:packages/flow-state-v3/src/core/cells.test.ts); the case-by-case comparison in @task.V3.T67.

    **Gates:**

    - `nub run faults`, which rejects the dead core and every named fault
      in code:packages/flow-state-v3/tests/faults.ts;
    - `nub run lint:rules`, which rejects the planted violations in code:tools/flow-state-lint/imports.test.ts
      and code:tools/flow-state-lint/rules.test.ts;
    - `nub run check`.

    **Failure limit:** 2.

    **Stops:**

    - a Pay Story that cannot pass across a reload (@task.V3.T63);
    - public entry-point names: `Story`, `Fake` and `propertyTest` follow @plan.Testing and stay unexported in this
      phase; exporting any of them, or naming the CLI's commands beyond the Plan's (@task.V3.T69), is the user's.

    **User's read:** the agent decisions in section 12 of the proposal; the Story and Fake API as built; each case the
    port drops, with its reason.

    **Draws from:**

    - skill:policy-verification (prove a suite; the coverage record);
    - skill:policy-testing (the requirements as failing checks first; audit a suite);
    - skill:execute-task and skill:check-task per Task; skill:review at each Task's close;
    - skill:policy-convergence at the threshold; skill:diagnose when a test fails unexplained;
    - the project's `effect-api-documentation` skill for every Effect API.
