            page, unknown value denied; C10 PAGE-2 shortcuts on every page, Run dark from the top; C11 PALETTE-1; C12
            PALETTE-2 (callback reason and index are view details); C13 PALETTE-3; C14 PALETTE-4 one call, row pending,
            rerun denied InFlight, settles; C15 PALETTE-5 denials stand for the prevented click; C16 dropped (onSelect
            and DOM Events); C17 PALETTE-6, also cleared on rerun; C18 PALETTE-7; C19 PALETTE-8; C20 dropped (element
            registration warning); C21 PALETTE-9; C22 PALETTE-10 denial stands for the unprevented key; C23 PALETTE-11
            list changed by `Configure`; C24 PALETTE-12; C25 dropped (controlled value, T30). Number: N1, N4, N5, N12
            dropped (formatting, part attributes, keyboard mode); N2 NUMBER-1 AtBound against Disabled; N3 NUMBER-2; N6
            NUMBER-3 values 7 then 10, one commit; N7 NUMBER-4 and N8 NUMBER-5 partial: values only, the shown "25%" is
            the view's; N9 NUMBER-6; N10 NUMBER-7; N11 NUMBER-8. Beyond upstream: NUMBER-9 to 12 (hold, bound, wheel,
            stress), PALETTE-13 (usual), PALETTE-14 (stress with reloads).
        comment     2026-11-15T22:11:23Z
            Review: PASS at 0b5c4b41 (independent; vp test 403 pass, check, lint:rules, check:plans, faults 51 of 51 and
            the dead core all green). No blocking finding: all 29 ports match upstream values; the C3, N7, N8 reductions
            are forced (score and shown text are not state; the RANK-3 order already proves accent folding and the
            prefix tier) and the 8 drops hold (N4's read-only lines assert part attributes only). Pins hold: upstream's
            own doc keeps errors per command; '70' commits 10; seq tells two equal commits apart. Routed to
            @task.V3.T70: drop `strideOf`, since the full sweep passes in about 5 s per test and needs only a test
            timeout; shortcutsOf lists disabled commands (upstream skips them); one frame stack instead of parallel
            `pages` and `queries`. For the user's read: NUMBER-10 commits at the bound's tick, as the proposal's table
